WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.024 --> 00:00:16.710
Ally hurried into her room and turned on Alpha.

2
00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:18.890
"I am Alpha."

3
00:00:20.551 --> 00:00:21.992
"Phew!" Ally said.

4
00:00:22.012 --> 00:00:24.973
"I'm glad you sound like yourself because I need your help."

5
00:00:26.013 --> 00:00:28.254
She filled Alpha in on all the team's problems.

6
00:00:28.274 --> 00:00:32.196
"We think Flo is the one spying on us."

7
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.261
"You are an Astralian, Allyzooba.

8
00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:38.581
Your prime directive is to help others," Alpha said.

9
00:00:39.722 --> 00:00:40.402
Ally frowned.

10
00:00:40.422 --> 00:00:44.963
"That's exactly what I'm trying to do—help my friends.

11
00:00:46.003 --> 00:00:48.684
But I can't levitate anything or read minds.

12
00:00:49.344 --> 00:00:50.985
My powers are gone!"

13
00:00:51.005 --> 00:00:56.826
"You were warned about becoming too human," Alpha said.

14
00:00:56.846 --> 00:00:59.347
"That's not helpful!"

15
00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:02.568
"Fine," Alpha said.

16
00:01:03.136 --> 00:01:04.057
"I will assist you."

17
00:01:04.517 --> 00:01:05.137
She paused.

18
00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.319
"Something helpful has occurred to me."

19
00:01:07.339 --> 00:01:10.261
"What?" Ally asked eagerly.

20
00:01:10.281 --> 00:01:14.484
"Even the noblest Astralians don't accomplish all of their missions.

21
00:01:15.384 --> 00:01:21.108
Sometimes all you can do is try your best and accept when you fail."

22
00:01:21.729 --> 00:01:22.429
Ally groaned.

23
00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:24.591
"That's not helpful either.

24
00:01:25.311 --> 00:01:29.974
Can you at least research what causes Astralians to lose their powers?"

25
00:01:31.295 --> 00:01:33.364
Alpha buzzed.

26
00:01:33.384 --> 00:01:34.966
"I found something that might apply.

27
00:01:35.786 --> 00:01:41.050
Astralians lose their powers when exposed to the effects of lunar yodel-lay-eh-hoo!"

28
00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:45.614
"What?" Ally shook Alpha.

29
00:01:46.094 --> 00:01:48.616
"When we're exposed to the effects of lunar what?"

30
00:02:03.084 --> 00:02:03.724
Alpha only yodeled loudly again.

31
00:02:03.744 --> 00:02:04.365
"Ugh!" Ally powered Alpha down.

32
00:02:04.385 --> 00:02:07.847
"Now I have something else to figure out— how to get a new device for you!"

33
00:02:07.867 --> 00:02:11.849
The next morning Ally was putting on her shoes when Mateo knocked on her door.

34
00:02:11.869 --> 00:02:15.391
"I just got a text from Barry," Mateo said.

35
00:02:15.411 --> 00:02:18.373
"He wants us to meet him at the truck.

36
00:02:18.793 --> 00:02:21.094
He said he has good news and bad news."

37
00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:24.216
"I'll be right out," Ally called back.

38
00:02:26.157 --> 00:02:27.778
Barry was waiting for them at the truck.

39
00:02:29.199 --> 00:02:30.500
"I won't keep you in suspense.

40
00:02:31.752 --> 00:02:33.734
The good news is the truck is fixed."

41
00:02:34.575 --> 00:02:35.436
Mateo cheered.

42
00:02:35.456 --> 00:02:43.183
"But the bad news is, it was definitely sabotage," Barry said.

43
00:02:43.203 --> 00:02:47.347
"Someone deliberately cut the power and fuel lines."

44
00:02:49.189 --> 00:02:49.810
Ally gulped.

45
00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:52.172
"Maybe we can't wait to set a trap.

46
00:02:53.093 --> 00:02:55.915
Maybe we'd better go talk to Flo right now!"

47
00:02:59.392 --> 00:03:03.155
When Ally, Mateo, and Barry got to the diner, it was almost empty.

48
00:03:03.856 --> 00:03:06.678
Flo was behind the counter, filling the napkin dispenser.

49
00:03:07.599 --> 00:03:08.720
Ally took a deep breath.

50
00:03:14.265 --> 00:03:15.806
we need to talk."

51
00:03:17.087 --> 00:03:18.008
"Sure, what's up?"

52
00:03:18.408 --> 00:03:19.089
Flo asked.

53
00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:23.413
"We know the truth about what you've been doing," Mateo said.

54
00:03:24.374 --> 00:03:25.735
Flo's eyes went wide.

55
00:03:25.755 --> 00:03:26.816
"You do?"

56
00:03:28.012 --> 00:03:31.193
"When Ray finds out, you'll have to quit, Flo," Barry said.

57
00:03:32.154 --> 00:03:34.595
"What?" Flo looked crestfallen.

58
00:03:34.615 --> 00:03:37.336
"I love my job here."

59
00:03:37.356 --> 00:03:40.977
"As much as you love spying on us for Pepe's?"

60
00:03:41.317 --> 00:03:42.058
Barry shouted.

61
00:03:43.518 --> 00:03:45.539
"Spying? For Pepe's?"

62
00:03:46.279 --> 00:03:47.460
Flo looked confused.

63
00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:49.441
"Why would you think that?"

64
00:03:49.461 --> 00:03:53.462
"Because somebody is stealing our recipes.

65
00:03:54.523 --> 00:03:58.489
And Julius and I saw you go to Pepe's," Ally said.

66
00:03:58.509 --> 00:04:01.151
"Why else would you go there?"

67
00:04:01.171 --> 00:04:03.873
"Why wouldn't I go there?"

68
00:04:04.253 --> 00:04:04.913
Flo asked.

69
00:04:04.933 --> 00:04:07.495
"My cousin works there.

70
00:04:08.076 --> 00:04:11.318
I went to bring her our grandmother's recipe for chicken soup."

71
00:04:12.339 --> 00:04:13.580
"Oh," Ally said.

72
00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:16.362
"But what about the eclipse?"

73
00:04:16.762 --> 00:04:17.503
Mateo asked.

74
00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:20.265
"Why did you ignore us that night at the park?"

75
00:04:21.426 --> 00:04:22.066
Flo shrugged.

76
00:04:22.086 --> 00:04:23.848
"I didn't see you there.

77
00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:29.662
I was with my cousin, and she got a text right after the eclipse that her mother-in-law had

78
00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:30.282
an accident.

79
00:04:30.682 --> 00:04:31.783
We left in a big hurry."

80
00:04:34.024 --> 00:04:35.604
Ally peered closely at Flo.

81
00:04:36.445 --> 00:04:37.905
She seemed to be telling the truth.

82
00:04:37.925 --> 00:04:44.128
"But you've been leaving work early a lot lately, and why wouldn't you sign the show's waiver?"

83
00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:52.211
like watching TV," Flo said.

84
00:04:52.231 --> 00:04:54.592
"But I don't want to be on it.

85
00:04:55.892 --> 00:04:58.013
And I've been pet-sitting for a friend.

86
00:04:59.213 --> 00:05:02.675
Her cat is sick, and I can't leave him alone for very long."

87
00:05:05.556 --> 00:05:06.816
Mateo looked relieved.

88
00:05:07.517 --> 00:05:08.557
"That makes sense."

89
00:05:09.978 --> 00:05:10.878
"It sure does!"

90
00:05:11.838 --> 00:05:13.539
Ally flung her arms around Flo.

91
00:05:13.559 --> 00:05:16.720
"Hooray! You're not the spy!"

92
00:05:18.201 --> 00:05:18.981
Barry frowned.

93
00:05:19.862 --> 00:05:21.542
"We still have a few problems, folks.

94
00:05:22.003 --> 00:05:23.583
Like what to serve for the contest.

95
00:05:23.843 --> 00:05:25.224
And who is the spy?"

96
00:05:26.428 --> 00:05:29.691
"I don't know anything about the spy," Flo said.

97
00:05:29.711 --> 00:05:35.476
"But for the contest, I think you should stick to the one thing that no one can steal."

98
00:05:35.496 --> 00:05:37.338
"What's that?"

99
00:05:37.658 --> 00:05:38.238
Ally asked.

100
00:05:38.258 --> 00:05:41.181
"Our reputation," Flo said.

101
00:05:41.201 --> 00:05:47.066
"Ray's is known for good food, good prices, and a friendly atmosphere.

102
00:05:48.187 --> 00:05:49.608
That's our winning formula.

103
00:05:50.189 --> 00:05:52.070
Why change it for the contest?"

104
00:05:54.524 --> 00:05:59.028
"Customers do love the Beta Burgana," Ally said slowly.

105
00:06:00.249 --> 00:06:01.810
She looked at Barry and Mateo.

106
00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:04.853
"Flo's right, let's stick with what works."

107
00:06:05.093 --> 00:06:06.334
Barry and Mateo nodded.

108
00:06:06.354 --> 00:06:10.898
"Now we have to solve two more problems," Mateo said.

109
00:06:10.918 --> 00:06:15.742
"Who's been spying on us—and who sabotaged the truck?"

110
00:06:15.762 --> 00:06:19.545
"I'm going to find out," Ally thought.

111
00:06:19.565 --> 00:06:22.588
"Even if I don't have any powers to do it with!"
